{{Documentation subpage}}

Given some wikitext, this template outputs both a text version with syntax highlighting and the output from the parser.

It avoid the duplication frequently seen in template documentation, where wikitext is written twice.

== Usage ==

===Simple usage===

<syntaxhighlight lang=wikitext>
{{T/Example|<nowiki>
{{Done}} and {{not done}}
</nowiki>}}
</syntaxhighlight>

The code above will produce the following:

{{T/Example|<nowiki>
{{Done}} and {{not done}}
</nowiki>}}

=== A more complicated template ===
The example below shows an infobox along with some custom HTML markup to prevent it from floating on the right of the page.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
{{T/Example|<nowiki>
<div style="max-width: fit-content">
{{LuaInfobox
|title=Li Shengwu
|Alma Mater :: University of Oxford<br/>Stanford University
|-header :: Scientific career
|Field :: Economics
|Institution :: Harvard University
}}
</div>
<div style="clear:both"/>
</nowiki>}}
</syntaxhighlight>

The code above is rendered as follows:

{{T/Example|<nowiki>
<div style="max-width: fit-content">
{{LuaInfobox
|title=Li Shengwu
|Alma Mater :: University of Oxford<br/>Stanford University
|-header :: Scientific career
|Field :: Economics
|Institution :: Harvard University
}}
</div>
<div style="clear:both"/>
</nowiki>}}

=== With the nowiki tag ===

If a complicated example has a <code><nowiki>&lt;/nowiki></nowiki></code> tag in it, we can escape it using <code><nowiki>&lt;//nowiki></nowiki></code>.

<syntaxhighlight lang=wikitext>
{{T/Example|1=<nowiki>{{Repeat

| pattern = <nowiki>
*{{TNAME}} (see {{tl|TNAME}})
<//nowiki>

| arg1 = TNAME

| Done
| Not done
| Comment

}}
</nowiki>}}
</syntaxhighlight>

Note the double slash inside the closing <code>nowiki</code> tag. The code above results in the following wikitext/result pair.

{{T/Example|1=<nowiki>{{Repeat

| pattern = <nowiki>
*{{TNAME}} (see {{tl|TNAME}})
<//nowiki>

| arg1 = TNAME

| Done
| Not done
| Comment

}}
</nowiki>}}

== Limitations ==
{{tl|T/Example}} cannot be used to show an example of using itself: this causes a template loop.

Some special characters may get escaped by the <code>nowiki</code> tag. The Lua module currently unescapes <code><</code> and <code>></code>. Please reach out to the author of this template if you notice other characters that need to be unescaped.

